CHAPTER VI
MINIMUM SERVICE STANDARDS
Article 10
The MSS for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence aims to guarantee that Women and Children victims of violence receive the minimum services needed.
The MSS for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence includes services for: handling complaints/reports of victims of violence against Women and Children;
health services for Women and Children victims of violence;
social rehabilitation for Women and Children victims of violence;
law enforcement and legal assistance for Women and Children victims of violence; and repatriation and social reintegration for Women and Children victims of violence.

1.2.text:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 5
Every Woman and Child Victim of Violence has the right: to have their dignity respected as a human being;
to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on a Protection order determination from the Court;
to Recovery of physical, psychological and sexual health services in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
to special handling related to victim confidentiality;
to assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
to spiritual guidance services; and to determine their own decisions.

Article 7
The community has the obligation and responsibility in providing Protection to Women and Child Victims of Violence.
The obligation and responsibility of the community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in the form of: preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against Women and Children;
providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against Women and Children to the authorized parties;
providing emergency assistance; and providing protection to victims of violence.

CHAPTER IV
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 6
The Regional Government has the authority and responsibility for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.
The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include: implementing policies for the protection of Women and Children victims of violence based on laws and regulations;
establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
allocating budget in the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence.

